<title>NETHERLANDS: HOCKEY-INTERNATIONAL FOUR-NATION MEN'S TOURNAMENT RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HOCKEY-INTERNATIONAL FOUR-NATION MEN'S TOURNAMENT RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the third and final day of the Rabobank International Trophy four-nation men's hockey tournament in Amstelveen on Sunday:</p>
<p>England 2 South Africa 2 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>England - Jon Wyatt 40, Calum Giles 66</p>
<p>South Africa - Craig Fulton 2, Greg Nicol 70  </p>
<p>Netherlands 4 Pakistan 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Remco van Wijk 27, Bram Lomans 45, 53, Stephan Veen</p>
<p>68</p>
<p>    Final standings   P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> Netherlands	    3   3   0   0  14    1   9</p>
<p> England		  3   1   1   1   6   10   4</p>
<p> Pakistan		 3   1   0   2   8   10   3</p>
<p> South Africa	   3   0   1   2   5   12   1</p>
